I have the PluginManager.cs code snippet and the context of the method calling ILogger.LogError. The key type LocalPlugin is referenced but not found in the Plugins folder. I want to write tests for the PluginManager.LoadAssemblies method, especially to cover the LogError calls on exceptions during assembly loading.

I will create a test class for PluginManager. To do so, I need to mock ILogger<PluginManager>, IServerApplicationHost, ServerConfiguration, and provide a plugin with DllFiles that will cause exceptions to trigger the LogError calls.

I will apply the make_virtual refactor to PluginManager.LoadAssemblies or the method that calls LogError so I can override or intercept behavior if needed. But since LoadAssemblies is public and calls ILogger directly, I can mock ILogger and verify LogError calls.

I will submit a test file with xUnit and Moq that tests the LoadAssemblies method, simulating the exception cases to cover the LogError calls on line 153 and others.

