The types LocalPlugin and PluginManifest are not found in the repo folders, likely they come from referenced assemblies or external packages. Since I cannot directly reference or instantiate LocalPlugin, I cannot create a fake subclass for it.

The PluginManager class is sealed and uses PluginLoadContext which is not virtual, so I cannot easily mock or override the assembly loading to simulate exceptions.

Given these constraints, I will write a test that verifies the LogError call by mocking ILogger and calling LoadAssemblies with a plugin that has a DLL file path that does not exist, expecting the assembly load to fail and LogError to be called.

I will create a minimal test that uses reflection to inject a fake plugin object with the necessary properties (using a dynamic or anonymous type) to trigger the error path and verify the logger call.

